<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gitega</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gitega is the political capital of Burundi and one of its largest cities, in the central highlands. A former royal centre and colonial administrative post, it houses the country's National Museum. In 2019 the government made it the political capital in place of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bujumbura">Bujumbura</a>, which remains the economic capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gitega.jpg" alt="Gitega" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NIHEREWENIMANA Richard · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dioc%C3%A8se_Gitega_y.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
